IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap1-logic`
IMPORT `snap1-s2014-abc`
IMPORT `snap1-s2014-e1`
IMPORT `snap1-s2014-e2`

-- Tests for 7 U.S.C. 2014(e). Expected values are written from the text (and the USDA's FY 2027 table) before the code was run.

§ `s 2014(e)(1) tests`

-- 8.31 percent of the income standard (c)(1), not more than 8.31 percent of the standard for 6 members, not less than the floor (217 in the 48 States, FY 2027).
-- size 4: 0.0831 x 2750 = 228.525 (above the floor); size 1: 0.0831 x 1330 = 110.523 (below the floor, so the floor); size 8: 0.0831 x 4644 is above the 6-member cap 0.0831 x 3697 = 307.2207.
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(A) the standard deduction` 2750 3697 217 EQUALS 228.525
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(A) the standard deduction` 1330 3697 217 EQUALS 217
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(A) the standard deduction` 4644 3697 217 EQUALS 307.2207
-- Guam: 8.31 percent of twice the 48-States standard. size 4: 0.0831 x 5500 = 457.05; size 1: 0.0831 x 2660 = 221.046 (below the 435 floor); size 8: capped at 0.0831 x 7394 = 614.4414.
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(B) the standard deduction for Guam` 2750 3697 435 EQUALS 457.05
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(B) the standard deduction for Guam` 1330 3697 435 EQUALS 435
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(B) the standard deduction for Guam` 4644 3697 435 EQUALS 614.4414
-- the floors for fiscal year 2009: $144, $246, $203, $127 and, for Guam, $289
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(I) the minimum standard deduction for fiscal year 2009` `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` EQUALS JUST 144
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(I) the minimum standard deduction for fiscal year 2009` `Alaska, urban` EQUALS JUST 246
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(I) the minimum standard deduction for fiscal year 2009` `Alaska, rural 1` EQUALS JUST 246
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(I) the minimum standard deduction for fiscal year 2009` `Alaska, rural 2` EQUALS JUST 246
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(I) the minimum standard deduction for fiscal year 2009` Hawaii EQUALS JUST 203
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(I) the minimum standard deduction for fiscal year 2009` `the Virgin Islands of the United States` EQUALS JUST 127
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(I) the minimum standard deduction for fiscal year 2009` Guam EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(B)(ii)(I) the minimum standard deduction for Guam for fiscal year 2009` EQUALS 289
-- indexing to "the nearest lower dollar increment": 217.4 x 1.02 = 221.748 -> 221; unchanged -> 217; x 1.005 = 218.085 -> 218; x 0.99 = 214.83 -> 214
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(II) the minimum standard deduction after indexing` 217.4 0.02 EQUALS 221
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(II) the minimum standard deduction after indexing` 217 0 EQUALS 217
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(II) the minimum standard deduction after indexing` 217 0.005 EQUALS 218
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(II) the minimum standard deduction after indexing` 217 (0 MINUS 0.01) EQUALS 214
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(B)(ii)(II) the Guam minimum standard deduction after indexing` 289 0.02 EQUALS 294
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(C) the adjustment conforms` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1)(C) the adjustment conforms` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the USDA's FY 2027 table (lines 76-81 of the COLA page); 6 or more members take the row marked 6
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` 1 EQUALS JUST 217
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` 3 EQUALS JUST 217
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` 4 EQUALS JUST 229
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` 5 EQUALS JUST 268
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` 6 EQUALS JUST 308
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` 12 EQUALS JUST 308
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 `Alaska, urban` 2 EQUALS JUST 371
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 `Alaska, rural 2` 6 EQUALS JUST 385
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 Guam 4 EQUALS JUST 457
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 Guam 1 EQUALS JUST 435
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 Hawaii 5 EQUALS JUST 309
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 Hawaii 6 EQUALS JUST 354
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 `the Virgin Islands of the United States` 4 EQUALS JUST 229
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 `the Virgin Islands of the United States` 1 EQUALS JUST 191
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2026 Hawaii 5 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` 2027 Hawaii 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- finding F-E1: the USDA's $229 for 4 members is 47.5 cents above 8.31 percent of the rounded Table 1 ($228.525); the Act states no rounding
#ASSERT 229 MINUS `s 2014(e)(1)(A) the standard deduction` 2750 3697 217 EQUALS 0.475

