§ `s 2014(e) net income tests`

-- A worked household: income 2000 after (d); standard 217; earned income deduction 20 percent of 1000 = 200; dependent care 100; child support 50; medical 65.
-- 2000 - (217 + 200 + 100 + 50 + 65) = 1368. Shelter 1500: 1500 - 0.5 x 1368 = 816, capped at 769 (FY 2027, 48 States, no elderly or disabled member): net income 1368 - 769 = 599.
#ASSERT `s 2014(e) the household's income after the deductions other than the shelter deduction` 2000 217 200 100 50 65 EQUALS 1368
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(6)(A) the excess shelter expense deduction before the maximum` 1500 1368 EQUALS 816
#ASSERT `s 2014(e)(6) the excess shelter expense deduction` 816 (`s 2014(e)(6)(B) capped at` 769) EQUALS JUST 769
#ASSERT `s 2014(e) the household's net income` 1368 (JUST 769) EQUALS JUST 599
#ASSERT `s 2014(e) the household's net income` 1368 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
